/athletes/122411"} "Bruno Fratus"] " were expected to be his biggest challengers, with his teammate, " [:a {:href "/athletes/147473"} "Michael Andrew"] ", also highly considered."] "\n\n" [:p {} "All the favorites qualified easily through both the heats and semi-finals, with Dressel leading both rounds with 21.32 in the heats and 21.42 in the semis. Manaudou was second in both rounds, while Fratus was third in the semis, and fourth in the heats, just behind Greece’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/125507"} "Kristian Golomeev"] ", co-silver medallist with Fratus at the 2019 Worlds."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the final Dressel had a relatively slow reaction time but his large frame and powerful kick off the blocks put him in the lead by 10 metres and he was never headed, finishing in a gold medal winning 21.07, an Olympic record. Behind him, Manaudou edged out Fratus for the silver, 21.55 – 21.57, while Andrew was another 0.03 back in fourth. For Dressel this was his third individual gold medal at Tokyo 2020, and his fifth overall, giving him seven gold medals at the 2016 and 2020 Olympics."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/136353"} "Caeleb Dressel"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "21.32 (1 h10)"] [:td {} "21.42 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "21.07 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/125884"} "Florent Manaudou"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} "21.65 (2 h10)"] 